<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22309" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incepto</span></b> , āre, v.
			freq. a.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to begin</i>, <i>undertake</i>, <i>attempt</i> (ante- and post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inceptas facinus facere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Curc. 1, 1, 23</span></i>
			; so, with <i>inf.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">loqui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Trin. 4, 3, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">canere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					1, 11, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quo iter inceptas?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Truc. 1, 2, 28</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quid inceptas?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Eun. 5, 8, 1</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Esp., <i>to begin business</i>, cum aliquo, i. e. <i>to quarrel</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si cum illo inceptas homine,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Phorm. 4, 3, 24</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
